# Sediment — optional configuration.
#
# You probably don't need this file. Default: run `pnpm dev`, then configure
# your LLM provider in the Settings UI (persisted to data/llm-config.json).
#
# Copy to `.env` only if you need one of the sections below. All values are
# optional; shell env vars always win.

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Developer / self-host settings — configurable ONLY via this file
# (no Settings UI). Ordered roughly most- to least-commonly used.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Ports ──
# SERVER_PORT=3001
# WEB_PORT=5173

# ── Network (outbound proxy) ──
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:1086

# ── Debug ──
# Dump the fully-assembled per-turn prompt to a readable sidecar log
# (data/logs) for inspection. Off by default; set to true when
# debugging prompt assembly.
# HUABU_DEBUG_PROMPT=true

# ── External ACP agents (Copilot, Claude Code, …) ──
# Pairing itself is done in the Settings popover → "External Agents";
# codes are ephemeral and never written to disk (no env override).
# `ACP_URL` is only honoured by the `start-agentlet-daemon` wrapper when
# pointing the local CLI at a remote / TLS-fronted Sediment instance.
# ACP_URL=wss://my.host/api/acp/agent

# ── Network exposure ──
# By default the server binds to 127.0.0.1 only, so a fresh install is
# never silently exposed to the LAN. Set HUABU_BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0 (or a
# specific NIC IP) to listen on every interface. When you do, you MUST
# also list every hostname/IP clients will use to reach the server in
# HUABU_ALLOWED_HOSTS — requests with any other Host header are
# rejected (defence against DNS rebinding). Pair both with
# HUABU_BASIC_AUTH_* and put HTTPS in front for anything beyond a
# trusted LAN.
# HUABU_BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0
# HUABU_ALLOWED_HOSTS=192.168.1.50,sediment.team-a.example

# ── Team share (HTTP Basic Auth on dev server) ──
# Both required. Plaintext — only safe on trusted network / behind HTTPS.
# HUABU_BASIC_AUTH_USER=
# HUABU_BASIC_AUTH_PASS=

# ── Managed workspace mode ──
# Locks workspace to this absolute path; disables folder picker.
# Unset = free mode (clients choose any directory).
# HUABU_WORKSPACE=/var/lib/sediment/team-a

# ── Standalone credential encryption ──
# Required only when credentials are saved through the Settings UI on a
# standalone server. Use the Base64 encoding of exactly 32 random bytes and
# keep it outside the data directory. Losing or changing this key makes the
# encrypted credentials unreadable. Electron uses OS safeStorage instead.
# Generate one with Node.js, then keep the output unchanged:
# node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
# HUABU_SECRET_KEY=


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# RECOMMENDED: configure everything below from the Settings UI
# (top-right gear). The env vars here are only headless/Docker
# fallbacks — a value saved in the UI always wins.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── LLM (Settings → LLM Provider) ──
# Set ONE key; server auto-selects on startup.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# Azure needs all three:
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_ENDPOINT=
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_DEPLOYMENT_NAME=
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-08-01-preview

# ── Web search — Tavily (Settings → Integrations) ──
# TAVILY_API_KEY=

# ── YouTube transcripts — RapidAPI (Settings → Integrations) ──
# RAPIDAPI_KEY=
